en:
Yes, that's right.
I didn't think much of it, so I didn't say anything.
I didn't want to say something weird and put a crack in our friendship.{p}

Lights-out came, and worn out from practice, we fell asleep right away.
It seemed some people stayed up talking late, but I fell asleep right away, too.
All I remember is a vague sense that Sodeyama was moaning in his sleep during the night.{p}

At training camp, you manage to get up even on mornings when you normally couldn't, don't you?
When it's time to get up, everything around you suddenly starts stirring.
Even I, who usually can hardly drag myself out of bed, managed to get up that day without much of a struggle.{p}

All through practice that day, Sodeyama looked like he was really suffering.
His shoulders drooped as if even breathing was hard for him, and he was drained the whole time.
The Sodeyama who used to answer me with a shy smile whenever I spoke to him had become a different person in just one day.{p}

He built a screen around an empty bed in the lodge and let her use it.
During the day he had her go somewhere else on the school grounds, and at night, once everyone was asleep, he let her back into the lodge.
She told him this.{p}

"You broke your promise..."
The Upside-Down Woman appeared behind Sodeyama.
And from behind, she...{p}

"Stop... gwaaah...!☆"
The Upside-Down Woman hacked Sodeyama's body apart, piece after piece.
His blood splashed all over my face, and I couldn't really tell what was happening.{p}

"Good, good, that's a good boy.
Just like you promised, don't you tell anyone..."
With that, the Upside-Down Woman slid away, vanishing as if climbing upward.{p}

If you sleep in the bed where Ono died, just his head floats up in front of you, glowing faintly.
And the eyes in that face dart around like a bug's, and the skin glitters like a bug's, too.
Just like a bug, it's the most brilliant color you've ever seen...{p}

I see...
I pray that curiosity of yours doesn't bring you misfortune down the road.
Then, instead of a bug story, shall I tell you an even more disgusting one?{p}

"Nobody should be using it until summer."
There were still students at school, busy with their club activities.
Takeda snuck into the lodge so that none of the other students would see her.{p}

"You'll be fine here.
I'll bring you something to eat again tomorrow."
With that, she went home for the day.{p}

The next day, she took the leftovers from her lunch and went to the lodge, making sure no one saw her.
"Sorry I'm late.
You must be starving."{p}

"So that's why you've been so weirdly cheerful lately, Naoko."
The girl gave a nasty smile.
Then she went back to class and told her friends all about it.{p}

The cats sank their teeth into her all over her body.
And when the cats pulled away, she collapsed, covered in blood.
Her bones were laid bare, and her guts were spilling out of her fallen body.{p}

After school, when Takeda went there, the kitten's corpse was lying on the floor.
"Who would... This is horrible..."
Takeda grieved.{p}

Then lights-out came, and the whole class went to bed.
Even after the lights were turned off, some people kept on chatting.
But before long, worn out from the day, everyone fell asleep.{p}

Suddenly, a cat cried out.
"Noooo!"
They all screamed at once.{p}

An ambulance was called right away, but she died on the spot.
The kitten that had jumped with her came through without a single scratch.
They say that until she was loaded into the ambulance, the kitten kept desperately licking the wounds on her corpse.{p}

"N-Naoko..."
Takeda was standing behind her.
They say Takeda smiled eerily with eyes like a cat's, and then sent the girl's head flying with something like a huge scythe.{p}

Since it's none of your business, you just say whatever comes to mind.
Watching from the safety of the stands, is that it?
I'm sure someone like you would never end up a loser, {a}.{p}

I put him to bed in my own bed.
I did hesitate, I'll admit.
Sodeyama slept like the dead.{p}

Then all of a sudden, the monster grew frightened.
It was an unexpected reaction.
So, taking a desperate gamble, I tried spitting at it.{p}

It's not as if I have no sense of responsibility, so I'll tell my story to the end.
But I'd like you to stop being so rude from now on.
Now then, I'll ask you once more.{p}

Then the monster put its mouth to Sodeyama's arm again and began to suck at it, slurp, slurp.
I don't know how much time passed.
After a while, the monster looked satisfied and quietly vanished.{p}

I can't even tell what he's saying anymore...
Hino...
Why did you invite someone like this...?{p}

"Everyone's already gone home.
You were asleep for so long.
Come on, let's go home too..."{p}
